MINI Project: File Auditor & Backup
Name: Sedra Mohamed Samir 
ID: 2406233
- I did the project solo. I implemented all the mentioned requirements in the PDF. Below is everything about the project, how to run it, and the prerequisites.

I) Project Overview
- This is a bash project that can audit files and directories, check their permissions, search for files, generate extension reports and back files up.

II) Files
- auditor.sh: Bash script.
- lib.sh: Contains helper functions.
- README.txt: Documentation.
- sample_data/: A directory containing files and directories for testing.

III) Functions
- Scan Directory: Lists files and directories and count them.
- Permission Audit: Checks write, read, and execute permissions.
- Extension Report: Counts the files according to their extension.
- Search File: Searches for a file by its name.
- Backup All: Creates a backup for timestamps of the readable files.
- List Backup: Displays all the backedup files.
- Restore Backup: Restores a given backup without overwriting the original file.

IV) How to run
- Open the directory and run the following:
1_ bash auditor.sh sample_data
(for the full list to appear)

2_ bash auditor.sh sample_data scan
   bash auditor.sh sample_data perms
   bash auditor.sh sample_data ext
   bash auditor.sh sample_data backup
(to use command-line arguments)

V) Prerequisites
- Ubuntu/Linux
- Bash shell
